Owner ruling (2026-11-02): third-party-tool packs such as CISA ScubaGear and ScubaGoggles do not ship inside Maester
(`packs/`). Each gets its own repository under maester365, one repo per pack (e.g. `maester365/maester-pack-scubagear`),
installed with `Install-MtPack maester365/<repo>`; IDs `maester365.<name>`, tests `MP.<Code>...`.

**Why:** they are not all Microsoft 365 (ScubaGoggles is Google Workspace), users add them by choice, and Maester picks a
pack's release per repository, so a shared packs repo would release every pack together.

**How to apply:** build such packs as installed packs (no reserved prefixes or docs in Maester). Keep the catalog
builder and Pester tests in the repo but `export-ignore` them in `.gitattributes`, because every .ps1 in a pack may
hold only functions and Install-MtPack checks GitHub's zipball. Codes: `SCUBA.M365` (ScubaGear), `SCUBA.GWS`
(ScubaGoggles). 2026-11-05: published as public https://github.com/maester365/maester-pack-scubagear (local clone
~/github/maester-pack-scubagear), CI green on Ubuntu and Windows; confirmed GitHub's zipball omits export-ignore paths.
No release yet (PACK_RELEASES unset), branch ruleset not applied, not yet run against real ScubaGear on Windows. ScubaGear 2.0 needs Windows PowerShell 5.1 for interactive sign-in; see [[maester-marketplace-design]].
